                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="542-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="542-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="542-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>ShuaiYin SYT-3000</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Multi-Pattern Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The SYT-3000 is a large-diaphragm tube mic. A pattern-selection switch on the front of the mic body offers cardioid, omni, and figure-of-8 pickup patterns. Two switches on the rear of the mic provide an attenuation pad and HPF.</p><blockquote><p><cite>ShuaiYin</cite></p><p>We use triode wiring on specially selected low-noise pentode vacuum tube (6J1) to yield low noise and incredibly realistic dynamic response.</p></blockquote><p>Internal shockmounting is claimed to make an external shockmount unnecessary; the SYT-3000 ships with a yoke mount.<p>The <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/ShuaiYin/SYT-3000">ShuaiYin SYT-3000</a> is also known as: SYT3000.</p>
